warheads and extending the MPT. And today, another&nbsp;
step of that openness is coming clean on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:05.584 --> 00:58:11.104
human radiation experience. When the president&nbsp;
appointed the advisory committee, he appointed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:11.104 --> 00:58:17.664
he committed our whole government to a massive&nbsp;
record search which included some 80 I'm sorry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:17.664 --> 00:58:26.944
some 840,000 pages on the declassification of some&nbsp;
3,020 documents. And we have made available to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:26.944 --> 00:58:31.984
American people these government records because&nbsp;
they strike at the heart of the relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:31.984 --> 00:58:37.184
between the American people and their government&nbsp;
and whether the government misused individual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:37.184 --> 00:58:42.384
citizens. The president committed to do this&nbsp;
without knowing where it would lead or whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:42.384 --> 00:58:48.464
the records would reveal government mistakes,&nbsp;
cause embarrassments or lawsuits. He did this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:48.464 --> 00:58:53.824
because he believed that it was the right thing&nbsp;
to do. Today, the president receives from Dr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:53.824 --> 00:58:59.264
Feden and her colleagues on the president's&nbsp;
advisory committee, a report that tells the story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:59.264 --> 00:59:06.224
of radiation experiments involving human subjects&nbsp;
funded by the government. We did not realize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:06.224 --> 00:59:13.184
when we began this journey the difficulty of the&nbsp;
charge given these citizens, imminent ethicists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:13.184 --> 00:59:21.984
physicians, scientists, citizens, even lawyers.&nbsp;
For the past 18 months, the advisory committee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:21.984 --> 00:59:27.424
members and their staff have devoted much&nbsp;
of their lives to this investigation. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:27.424 --> 00:59:33.264
sacrificed their weekends, their vacations, and&nbsp;
late hours. And in the end, for the committee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:33.264 --> 00:59:39.584
their actual working days to review the&nbsp;
documents going back for decades. Today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:39.584 --> 00:59:46.384
they give us their best judgment as to whether&nbsp;
persons were wronged. The nation owes to them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:46.384 --> 00:59:53.664
to their families, and to all the staffs that have&nbsp;
worked on this issue, the generous gratitude for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:53.664 --> 00:59:59.424
their public service, and most importantly for the&nbsp;
recommendations which the president will receive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:59.424 --> 01:00:10.064
shortly. And most of all, we owe a gracious thanks&nbsp;
to the family members who are here. Dr. Fayen

01:00:20.304 --> 01:00:28.544
Mr. President, Secretary Olyri, Attorney General&nbsp;
Reno, Secretary Shala, other members of the human&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:28.544 --> 01:00:35.184
radiation inter agency working group. On behalf&nbsp;
of my 13 colleagues on the advisory committee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:35.184 --> 01:00:42.784
I am proud to submit our final report. We worked&nbsp;
extremely hard over the last 18 months in order&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:42.784 --> 01:00:48.784
to inform you and the American people about what&nbsp;
really happened to radiation research subjects&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:48.784 --> 01:00:54.944
in the Cold War period. With the assistance of&nbsp;
federal agencies, private research centers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:00:54.944 --> 01:01:01.904
hospitals and numerous citizens, we have assembled&nbsp;
and reviewed hundreds of thousands of documents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:01.904 --> 01:01:06.864
many of which were previously secret.&nbsp;
In 31 days of open hearings conducted&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:06.864 --> 01:01:13.744
in Washington and throughout the country, we&nbsp;
have heard from hundreds of public witnesses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:13.744 --> 01:01:20.704
we have found that wrongs were indeed committed&nbsp;
both with experiments involving radiation and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:20.704 --> 01:01:27.024
with intentional releases of radiation into&nbsp;
the environment. In the pursuit of peace and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:27.024 --> 01:01:34.064
the advancement of medicine, certainly to laudable&nbsp;
goals, the rights and interests of individuals and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:34.064 --> 01:01:40.464
communities were sometimes ignored. We found&nbsp;
that government officials and physicians who&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:40.464 --> 01:01:47.904
had the trust of the public and of their patients&nbsp;
abused that trust. Patients were used as subjects&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:47.904 --> 01:01:54.304
of experiments without their knowledge or consent.&nbsp;
Information was withheld from affected communities&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:54.304 --> 01:01:59.264
and from the public. Secrets were kept to&nbsp;
protect the government from embarrassment&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:59.264 --> 01:02:06.064
and legal liability. While the radiation doses&nbsp;
in the experiments we studied were usually low,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:06.064 --> 01:02:12.784
and officials and scientists were often concerned&nbsp;
about risk, we do not believe that excuses the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:12.784 --> 01:02:20.144
wrongs that were done. We urge you to do the right&nbsp;
thing by those who have been wronged or harmed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:20.144 --> 01:02:26.704
these events. In our report, we recommend for&nbsp;
your consideration guidelines for compensating&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:26.704 --> 01:02:35.904
former subjects. But if we are to keep faith with&nbsp;
those who have suffered, we must all do more. Your&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:35.904 --> 01:02:41.424
extraordinary efforts have allowed the American&nbsp;
people to learn about a piece of our history&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:41.424 --> 01:02:47.904
that we could not otherwise have understood. You&nbsp;
have opened the doors of this nation's records,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:47.904 --> 01:02:55.824
and they must stay open. You have recognized&nbsp;
the price of secrecy in research for what it is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:55.824 --> 01:03:03.744
a legacy of cynicism and a legacy of distrust. If&nbsp;
we are to keep faith with those who have suffered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:03.744 --> 01:03:11.344
we must do everything possible to guarantee that&nbsp;
what happened to them never happens again. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:11.344 --> 01:03:16.064
committee learned that research safeguards&nbsp;
have come a long way since the Second World&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:16.064 --> 01:03:22.624
War. Americans can and should feel much&nbsp;
more secure about medical research today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:22.624 --> 01:03:29.264
but the system remains imperfect. I urge you&nbsp;
to carefully review the committee's findings&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:29.264 --> 01:03:35.264
and recommendations. Both the government and&nbsp;
research institutions must do all they can&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:35.264 --> 01:03:41.184
to protect our fellow citizens. If this&nbsp;
committee's work is to mean anything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:41.184 --> 01:03:47.744
it has to be that 50 years from now there does&nbsp;
not have to be another presidential committee&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:47.744 --> 01:03:53.264
charged with investigating al allegations of&nbsp;
abuses of human subjects. There should never&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:53.264 --> 01:04:00.304
be another such advisory committee. Information&nbsp;
must not be concealed again from people in their&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:00.304 --> 01:04:07.824
own time so that it takes two generations for the&nbsp;
truth to come out. Mr. President, your leadership&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:07.824 --> 01:04:13.344
in this area has been indispensable. Without&nbsp;
your willingness to open government files to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:13.344 --> 01:04:19.264
our scrutiny, our work would have been totally&nbsp;
impossible. We could not have done it. Your staff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:19.264 --> 01:04:24.784
your cabinet and agency heads and their staffs&nbsp;
have been supportive at every turn. We have had&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:24.784 --> 01:04:33.104
every request met, but always with great respect&nbsp;
for our independence. You've set a new standard&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:33.104 --> 01:04:40.224
for open government in an area that has been&nbsp;
largely secret for 50 years. We on the committee&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:40.224 --> 01:04:46.224
are both honored and grateful that you have taken&nbsp;
our work so seriously. I hope that we have met the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:46.224 --> 01:04:52.464
challenge that you put before us 18 months ago.&nbsp;
On behalf of the committee and of our staff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:04:52.464 --> 01:05:08.544
thank you for this extraordinary opportunity to&nbsp;
serve our nation. It has been a true privilege.

01:05:18.144 --> 01:05:22.864
We have some more people on the committee.

01:05:22.864 --> 01:05:26.704
Will the other committee members&nbsp;
uh please stand? Let's give them&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:26.704 --> 01:05:33.424
all a hand. They did an extraordinary job.

01:05:39.984 --> 01:05:51.104
Let me um begin with a simple thank you&nbsp;
to everyone who participated in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:51.104 --> 01:05:57.904
extraordinary project and to everyone who&nbsp;
supported them. Uh I am especially glad to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:05:57.904 --> 01:06:03.664
see here today uh Senator Glenn who's been&nbsp;
so active in working on the medical ethics&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:03.664 --> 01:06:12.144
issue. Uh Congressman Marky who's worked on this&nbsp;
issue for a very long time. Congressman Frost,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:12.144 --> 01:06:16.624
Secretary Shala, Deputy Secretary&nbsp;
of Veterans Affairs, Hershel Gober,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:16.624 --> 01:06:26.384
and of course the Attorney General basically tries&nbsp;
to get us all to do the right thing all the time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:27.424 --> 01:06:35.344
I want to thank uh I want to thank Secretary&nbsp;
Olri for her extraordinary devotion to this&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:35.344 --> 01:06:43.904
cause and you heard in her remarks basically&nbsp;
the the way that she views this. It's a part&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:43.904 --> 01:06:52.704
of her ongoing commitment to finish the end of the&nbsp;
cold war. and uh perhaps no energy secretary has&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:52.704 --> 01:06:58.384
ever done as much as she has to be an advocate&nbsp;
whether it is for uh continued reforms within&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:06:58.384 --> 01:07:03.504
the energy department or her outspoken endorsement&nbsp;
of the strongest possible commitment on the part&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:03.504 --> 01:07:08.384
of the United States to a comprehensive testban&nbsp;
treaty which I believe we will achieve next year&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:08.384 --> 01:07:14.704
in no small measure thanks to the support&nbsp;
of the secretary of energy and of course&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:14.704 --> 01:07:24.304
uh I want to thank Dr. Ruth Feden uh for her&nbsp;
extraordinary commitment of about a year and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:24.304 --> 01:07:32.944
a half of her life to this unusual but important&nbsp;
task. And all of you who served on the committee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:32.944 --> 01:07:37.584
I remember the first time we put this committee&nbsp;
together, I looked I said that's a pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:37.584 --> 01:07:43.824
distinguished outfit. I wish I could give them&nbsp;
five or six jobs to do. Thank you. I'll expect&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:43.824 --> 01:07:52.464
you back next Monday and we'll I I do thank you so&nbsp;
much for the work you have done. Let me tell you&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:07:52.464 --> 01:08:04.624
that just as this is an important part of u the&nbsp;
efforts that Secretary Olri outlined. I saw this&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:04.624 --> 01:08:12.224
committee as an indispensable part of our effort&nbsp;
to restore the confidence of the American people&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:12.224 --> 01:08:20.864
in the integrity of their government. All of these&nbsp;
political reform issues to me are are integrated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:20.864 --> 01:08:26.704
When I became the president, I realized we had&nbsp;
great new economic challenges. We had profound&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:26.704 --> 01:08:33.104
social problems. that a lot of these things had&nbsp;
to be done by an energized American citizenry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:33.104 --> 01:08:37.184
but that our national government had a role to&nbsp;
play in moving our country through this period&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:37.184 --> 01:08:42.704
of transition. And in order to do it, we needed&nbsp;
to increase the capacity of the government to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:42.704 --> 01:08:48.064
do it through political reform. But we also&nbsp;
needed, as much as anything else, to increase&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:48.064 --> 01:08:53.184
the confidence of the American people that at&nbsp;
the very least they could trust the United States&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:53.184 --> 01:08:59.984
government to tell the truth and to do the right&nbsp;
things. So, you have to understand that for me,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:08:59.984 --> 01:09:06.144
one reason this is so important is that I see&nbsp;
it as part of our ongoing effort to give this&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:06.144 --> 01:09:12.624
government back to the American people. Senator&nbsp;
Glenn's long effort to get Congress to apply to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:12.624 --> 01:09:18.464
itself the same laws it imposes on the private&nbsp;
sector. Uh the restrictions that I impose on&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:18.464 --> 01:09:23.344
members of my administration in high positions&nbsp;
for lobbying for foreign governments. And when the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:23.344 --> 01:09:29.504
lobby bill failed in the Congress, I just impose&nbsp;
it by executive order on members of the executive&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:29.504 --> 01:09:37.744
branch. Uh all these efforts at political reform,&nbsp;
it seems to me, are important. But none of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:37.744 --> 01:09:43.344
efforts can succeed unless people believe that&nbsp;
they can rely on their government to tell them&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:43.344 --> 01:09:49.424
the truth and to do the right thing. We have&nbsp;
declassified thousands of government documents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:49.424 --> 01:09:55.344
files from the Second World War, the Cold War.&nbsp;
President Kennedy's assassination. These actions&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:09:55.344 --> 01:10:00.624
are not only consistent with our national&nbsp;
security, they are essential to advance our&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:00.624 --> 01:10:08.464
values. So to me, that's what this is all about.&nbsp;
And to all those who represent the families who&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:08.464 --> 01:10:15.344
have been involved in these incidents, let me say&nbsp;
to you, I hope you feel that your government has&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:15.344 --> 01:10:20.944
kept its commitment to the American people&nbsp;
to tell the truth and to do the right thing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:21.824 --> 01:10:29.424
We discovered soon after I entered office that&nbsp;
with the spectre of an atomic war looming like&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:29.424 --> 01:10:36.384
Armageddon far nearer than it does today,&nbsp;
the United States government actually did&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:36.384 --> 01:10:43.104
carry out on our citizens experiments involving&nbsp;
radiation. That's when I ordered the creation of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:43.104 --> 01:10:51.584
this committee. Dr. Feden and the others uh did a&nbsp;
superb job. They enlisted the many of our nation's&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:51.584 --> 01:10:57.264
most significant and important medical and&nbsp;
scientific ethicists. They had to determine first&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:10:57.264 --> 01:11:04.864
whether experiments conducted or sponsored by our&nbsp;
government between 1944 and 1974 met the ethical&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:04.864 --> 01:11:11.024
and scientific standards of that time and of our&nbsp;
time. And then they had to see to it that our&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:11.024 --> 01:11:18.064
research today lives up to nothing less than our&nbsp;
highest values and our most deeply held beliefs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:18.704 --> 01:11:24.064
From the beginning, it was obvious to me that&nbsp;
this energetic committee was prepared to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:24.064 --> 01:11:30.864
its part. We declassified thousands of pages of&nbsp;
documents. We gave committee members the keys&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:30.864 --> 01:11:35.504
to the government's doors, file cabinets,&nbsp;
and safes. For the last year and a half,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:35.504 --> 01:11:41.104
the only thing that stood between them, and the&nbsp;
truth were all the late nights and hard work they&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:41.104 --> 01:11:51.984
had to put in. This report I received today is&nbsp;
a monumental document in more ways than one. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:11:51.984 --> 01:12:00.544
it is a very very important piece of America's&nbsp;
history and it will shape America's future in&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:00.544 --> 01:12:08.784
ways that will make us a more honorable,&nbsp;
more successful and more ethical country.

01:12:10.464 --> 01:12:17.184
What this committee learned I would like to review&nbsp;
today with a little more detail than Dr. Feden&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:17.184 --> 01:12:24.704
said because I think it must be engraved on our&nbsp;
national memory. Thousands of government sponsored&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:24.704 --> 01:12:30.224
experiments did take place at hospitals,&nbsp;
universities, and military bases around our&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:30.224 --> 01:12:37.424
nation. The goal was to understand the effects of&nbsp;
radiation exposure on the human body. While most&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:37.424 --> 01:12:43.824
of the tests were ethical by any standards, some&nbsp;
were unethical. Not only by today's standards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:43.824 --> 01:12:50.224
but by the standards of the time in which they&nbsp;
were conducted. They failed both the test of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:50.224 --> 01:12:57.264
our national values and the test of humanity. In&nbsp;
one experience, scientist experiment, scientists&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:12:57.264 --> 01:13:05.344
injected plutonium into 18 patients without their&nbsp;
knowledge. In another, doctors exposed indigent&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:05.344 --> 01:13:12.144
cancer patients to excessive doses of radiation,&nbsp;
a treatment from which it is virtually impossible&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:12.144 --> 01:13:17.984
that they could ever benefit. The report also&nbsp;
demonstrates that these and other experiments were&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:17.984 --> 01:13:25.824
carried out on precisely those citizens who count&nbsp;
most on the government for its help, the destitute&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:25.824 --> 01:13:33.184
and the gravely ill. But the dispossessed were not&nbsp;
alone. members of the military, precisely those on&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:33.184 --> 01:13:40.704
whom we in our government count most. They were&nbsp;
also test subjects. Informed consent means your&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:40.704 --> 01:13:45.824
doctor tells you the risk of the treatment&nbsp;
you are about to undergo. In too many cases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:45.824 --> 01:13:51.744
informed consent was withheld. Americans were&nbsp;
kept in the dark about the effects of what was&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:51.744 --> 01:13:57.504
being done to them. The deception extended beyond&nbsp;
the test subjects themselves to encompass their&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:13:57.504 --> 01:14:03.904
families and the American people as a whole. For&nbsp;
these experiments were kept secret and they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:03.904 --> 01:14:10.544
shrouded not for a compelling reason of national&nbsp;
security but for the simple fear of embarrassment&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:10.544 --> 01:14:17.824
and that was wrong. Those who led the government&nbsp;
when these decisions were made are no longer&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:17.824 --> 01:14:23.984
here to take responsibility for what they did.&nbsp;
They're not here to apologize to the survivors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:23.984 --> 01:14:29.824
the family members, or the communities whose lives&nbsp;
were darkened by the shadow of the atom and these&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:29.824 --> 01:14:36.464
choices. So today, on behalf of another generation&nbsp;
of American leaders and another generation of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:36.464 --> 01:14:44.224
American citizens, the United States of America&nbsp;
offers a sincere apology to those of our citizens&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:44.224 --> 01:14:50.464
who were subjected to these experiments, to&nbsp;
their families, and to their communities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:50.464 --> 01:14:57.504
When the government does wrong, we have a moral&nbsp;
responsibility to admit it. The duty we owe to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:14:57.504 --> 01:15:03.984
one another to tell the truth and to protect our&nbsp;
fellow citizens from excesses like these is one&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:03.984 --> 01:15:10.704
we can never walk away from. Our government&nbsp;
failed in that duty and it offers an apology&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:10.704 --> 01:15:16.624
to the survivors and their families and to all&nbsp;
the American people who must who must be able&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:16.624 --> 01:15:24.864
to rely upon the United States to keep its word to&nbsp;
tell the truth and to do the right thing. We know&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:24.864 --> 01:15:32.784
there are moments when words alone are not enough.&nbsp;
That's why I'm instructing my cabinet to use and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:32.784 --> 01:15:40.464
build on these recommendations to devise promptly&nbsp;
a system of relief, including compensation that&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:40.464 --> 01:15:46.624
meets the standards of justice and conscience.&nbsp;
When called for, we will work with Congress to&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:46.624 --> 01:15:53.584
serve the best needs of those who were harmed.&nbsp;
Make no mistake, as the committee report says,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:53.584 --> 01:15:59.744
there are circumstances where compensation is&nbsp;
appropriate as a matter of ethics and principle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:15:59.744 --> 01:16:06.384
I am committed to seeing to it that the United&nbsp;
States of America lives up to its responsibility.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:06.384 --> 01:16:12.944
Our greatness is measured not only in how we&nbsp;
so frequently do right, but also how we act&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:12.944 --> 01:16:19.424
when we know we've done the wrong thing. how&nbsp;
we confront our mistakes, make our apologies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:19.424 --> 01:16:25.424
and take action. That's why this morning I&nbsp;
signed an executive order instructing every&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:25.424 --> 01:16:32.064
arm and agency of our government that conducts,&nbsp;
supports, or regulates research involving human&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:32.064 --> 01:16:38.784
beings to review immediately their procedures&nbsp;
in light of the recommendations of this report&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:38.784 --> 01:16:45.424
and the best knowledge and standards available&nbsp;
today and to report back to me by Christmas.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:45.424 --> 01:16:50.864
I have also created a bioeththics advisory&nbsp;
commission to supervise the process to watch&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:50.864 --> 01:16:57.184
over all such research and to see to it that&nbsp;
never again do we stray from the basic values&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:16:57.184 --> 01:17:04.464
of protecting our people and being straight&nbsp;
with them. The report I received today will&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:04.464 --> 01:17:11.184
not be left on a shelf to gather dust. Every one&nbsp;
of its pages offers a lesson, and every lesson&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:11.184 --> 01:17:17.344
will be learned from these good people who put&nbsp;
a year and a half of their lives into the effort&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:17.344 --> 01:17:23.744
to set America straight. Medical and scientific&nbsp;
progress depends upon learning about people's&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:23.744 --> 01:17:29.744
responses to new medicines, to new cutting edge&nbsp;
treatments. Without this kind of research, our&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:29.744 --> 01:17:35.824
children would still be dying from polio and other&nbsp;
killers. Without responsible radiation research,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:35.824 --> 01:17:42.704
we wouldn't be making the progress we are in the&nbsp;
war on cancer. We have to continue to research.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:42.704 --> 01:17:49.104
But there is a right way and a wrong way to do it.&nbsp;
There are there are local citizens review boards.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:49.104 --> 01:17:53.744
There are regulations that establish proper&nbsp;
informed consent and ensure that experiments&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:17:53.744 --> 01:18:00.224
are conducted ethically. But in overseeing this&nbsp;
necessary research, we must never relax our&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:00.224 --> 01:18:06.224
vigilance. The breathtaking advances in science&nbsp;
and technology demand that we always keep our&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:06.224 --> 01:18:13.024
ethical watch light burning. No matter how rapid&nbsp;
the pace of change, it can never outrun our core&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:13.024 --> 01:18:20.624
convictions that have stood us so well as a nation&nbsp;
for more than 200 years now through many different&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:20.624 --> 01:18:27.264
scientific revolutions. I believe we will meet the&nbsp;
test of our times. that as science and technology&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:27.264 --> 01:18:35.424
evolve, our ethical conscience will grow, not&nbsp;
shrink. Informed consent, community right to know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:35.424 --> 01:18:40.864
our entire battery of essential human protections,&nbsp;
all these grew up in response to the health and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:40.864 --> 01:18:48.864
humanitarian crises of this 20th century. They&nbsp;
are proof that we are equal to our challenges.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:48.864 --> 01:18:56.704
Science is not ever simply objective. It emerges&nbsp;
from the crucible of historical circumstances and&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:18:56.704 --> 01:19:03.264
personal experience. Times of crisis and fear can&nbsp;
call forth bad science, even science we know in&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:03.264 --> 01:19:09.984
retrospect to be unethical. Let us remember the&nbsp;
difficult years chronicled in this report. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:09.984 --> 01:19:17.584
think about how good people could have done things&nbsp;
that we know were wrong. Let these pages serve as&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:17.584 --> 01:19:26.384
an internal reminder to hold humility and moral&nbsp;
accountability in higher esteem than we do the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:26.384 --> 01:19:34.304
latest development in technology. Let us remember&nbsp;
too that cynicism about government has roots in&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:34.304 --> 01:19:41.024
historical circumstances because of stonewallings&nbsp;
and evasions in the past. times when a family&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:41.024 --> 01:19:45.504
member or a neighbor suffered an injustice and&nbsp;
had nowhere to turn and couldn't even get the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:45.504 --> 01:19:53.264
facts. Some Americans lost faith in the promise&nbsp;
of our democracy. Government was very powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:19:53.264 --> 01:20:01.824
but very far away and not trusted to be ethical.&nbsp;
So today, by making ourselves accountable for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:01.824 --> 01:20:09.184
sins of the past, I hope more than anything else,&nbsp;
we are laying the foundation stone for a new era.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:09.904 --> 01:20:14.224
Good people like these members of Congress&nbsp;
who have labored on this issue for a long&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:14.224 --> 01:20:19.504
time and have devoted their careers to&nbsp;
trying to do the right thing and having&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:19.504 --> 01:20:27.104
people justifiably feel confidence in the work of&nbsp;
their representatives. They will continue to work&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:27.104 --> 01:20:33.344
to see that we implement these recommendations.&nbsp;
And under our watch, we will no longer hide the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:33.344 --> 01:20:41.104
truth from our citizens. We will act as if all&nbsp;
that we do will see the light of day. Nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:41.104 --> 01:20:46.944
that happens in Washington will ever be more&nbsp;
important in anyone's life affected by these&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:46.944 --> 01:20:53.424
experiments perhaps than these reports we issue&nbsp;
today. But all of us as Americans will be better&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:53.424 --> 01:20:59.104
off because of the larger lesson we learned&nbsp;
in this exercise and because of our continuing&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:20:59.104 --> 01:21:18.864
effort to demonstrate to our people that we can&nbsp;
be faithful to their values. Thank you very much.

